  "reading": "The network learns the primitive task and does not transfer it. Prefix-and-class languages in the training alphabet reach 0.844 balanced (AUROC 0.901). On the shifted split the selected checkpoint scores 0.556 balanced (AUROC 0.590) against 0.716 for the structural heuristic and 0.820 for the code-length rule. Where a query actually contains a held-out delimiter byte, balanced accuracy is 0.521 and true members are accepted only 24.7% of the time: an unfamiliar byte is treated as evidence against membership, rather than as a delimiter that is constant across the support. In-distribution full schemas reach 0.632 against the heuristic's 0.774. BENCH-C, scored once, is 0.508 against 0.935. The model is right on 60.4% of the heuristic's mistakes and on 53.7% of the heuristic's successes, so it is not a residual corrector either. Stage 1 does not yet show a language representation that a regex decoder can sit on.",
